test-core	Portable package tests (core scope; the list and its guards live in scripts/portable-tests.sh)	2026-11-14T03:08:05.1297852Z portable-tests.sh:   TestCanonicalizeErrorNoticeMustNotRelayTheFiledPath174r3 [fixture] ticket174 AC#6 shape 甲 (the ledger row, not the POSIX-equivalent shape 乙). The case is AC#2d's junction arm: the filed path must be a REAL NTFS junction (cmd /c mklink /J) whose link spelling C26 refuses - per the fixture comment (task_output_pointer_notice_test.go:376-380) a non-exempt reparse traversal is the ONLY reachable input that gives this branch a path literal at all. On POSIX nothing can be refused, because the detection it exercises is a Windows implementation (risk/pathresolver_other.go reparseComponents returns nil elsewhere - the same wall the workspace-junction row above names), so this machine has no subject: task_output_pointer_notice_test.go:408 skips with 前置条件缺失：造不出真 NTFS junction（mklink /J %s %s: %v: %s）, and the %v the ubuntu leg filled in was exec: "cmd": executable file not found in $PATH: (archived run-37166458550-failed.log, the file then at :428 - the line moves as other criteria land, so the row quotes the skip rather than the line). It RUNS AND PASSES on windows (real mklink /J, no skip), so the assertion is not lost, it is only un-evaluable here. Registered rather than deleted because runtests.sh makes every SKIP fatal (ticket 71 AC#3) and one unaccounted skip is exactly what turned test-core step7 red in the archived run (four numbers there: PASS=1010 FAIL=4 SKIP=1 - the FAILs have their own owners, the SKIP=1 is what this row accounts for): -skip filters an accounted name silently, so this is the repo's chosen mechanism for declaring the skip and re-checking it every run instead of letting it land as an unnamed red. OWNER of the POSIX half: whoever lands AC#6 shape 乙 on ticket 174, a POSIX-runnable equivalent of the same criterion (the notice may not relay the filed path, no junction needed); this row does not fake that half. Re-verified against the compiled LINUX test binary every run: delete the skip and the case starts running here; delete the case and the staleness check goes red. next= on ticket 174
